1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,583
Pirates. The plank. Walk!

2
00:00:02,733 --> 00:00:05,317
Nope. It almost never happened.

3
00:00:05,467 --> 00:00:07,517
Pirates: the plank myth.

4
00:00:07,667 --> 00:00:10,650
Pirates wanted ships and cargo.

5
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,350
Most crews just surrendered.

6
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,250
A plank ceremony? Too much work.

7
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:19,250
If a pirate wanted someone gone...

8
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,983
...they'd just throw them overboard.

9
00:00:22,133 --> 00:00:25,417
Or leave them on an island. Marooning.

10
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:28,283
So is the plank totally fake?

11
00:00:28,433 --> 00:00:31,417
Not totally. There are a few reports.

12
00:00:31,567 --> 00:00:34,383
Mostly from the 1800s.

13
00:00:34,533 --> 00:00:38,350
After the golden age of piracy had ended.

14
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,950
So where did the plank come from?

15
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,250
Stories and pictures.

16
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:47,117
Then Peter Pan. Captain Hook loves a plank.

17
00:00:47,267 --> 00:00:50,317
Now every pirate movie has one.

18
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:54,883
Golden age plank walks on record: basically zero.

19
00:00:55,033 --> 00:00:57,783
On screen? Plank walks everywhere.

20
00:00:57,933 --> 00:01:01,417
Anyway, here's a pirate with his plank.
